"The patient underwent a robot-assisted radical prostatectomy with a pathological stage of pT2, negative surgical margins, and no invasion of the seminal vesicles. The surgical pathology report documented \"no lymph node metastasis.\" Preoperative PSA was 4.3. The surgical findings, including Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2), negative margins, and absence of lymph node metastasis, are favorable prognostic factors. Countervailing findings include the preoperative PSA level and the fact that the biopsy report lacked a Gleason pattern and ISUP report. Nodal status is documented as negative, which is a positive finding. The prognosis is supported by the negative margins and absence of lymph node metastasis. Information that would revise this prognosis, particularly the postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory, is currently unknown as postoperative PSA or follow-up data are not recorded. The fixed estimated horizon is 81.76 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 65.41–98.11 months; its coverage has not been validated."
